<title>SPAIN: BCH 96 Net attributable up 169 pct. [CORRECTED 14:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>BCH 96 Net attributable up 169 pct. [CORRECTED 14:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects percentage in headline to 169 pct from 69 pct)</p>
<p>Full year 1996 results to end December for Spanish bank Banco Central Hispano</p>
<p>				    (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		 33.50  vs   12.47</p>
<p> Net profit				  44.09  vs   17.04</p>
<p> Pretax profit			     51.05  vs   21.14</p>
<p> Net interest income		    283.71  vs  250.91</p>
<p> Operating income			 386.74  vs  342.47</p>
<p> Operating profit			 101.27  vs   82.30</p>
<p>NOTE: BCH said it would pay a total dividend of 110 pesetas in 1996 after 75 pesetas in 1995.</p>
</text>
